course: dictionary
lesson: 2063
title: Thinking words: consider
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Consider is a thinking word. To consider something is to think about it carefully, usually before you decide. «Saying "we had not considered that" impresses more than bluffing» means the speaker thought about the idea properly before they spoke.
explain: Read the words around it to check. «A long list is easier in groups by meaning: time words, place words, thinking words (believe, consider, imagine).» Consider sits in the same group as believe and imagine, so it is a word about thinking.
explain: Consider can also mean think of someone as something, or think about how someone feels. In maths and exams, «Consider the number 24» means look at it and work with it.
fact: Consider means to think about something carefully, especially before you decide.
fact: «To consider someone to be something» means to think of them that way: «I consider her my best friend».
fact: To consider other people is to think about their feelings.
fact: In exams, «Consider the triangle ABC» means look at the triangle and work with it.
fact: «All things considered» means after thinking about everything.
exercise: «Consider all the answers before you choose.» What does consider mean here? | Shout them out loud | Count them quickly | Throw them away without looking | *Think about them carefully before deciding
exercise: «I consider her my best friend.» What does consider show? | She is a stranger to me | *She is someone I think of as my best friend | She is tired | She is my teacher
exercise: In a maths question you read «Consider the number 24». What should you do? | *Look at the number 24 and work with it | Rub it out | Write it in capital letters | Ignore it and move on
test: What does «consider other people's feelings» mean? | Forget them quickly | *Think about how they feel | Tell them to be quiet | Ask them to leave
test: «All things considered, the trip was a good idea.» What does all things considered mean? | Nothing was thought about at all | Everything was cancelled | *After thinking about everything | Only the first thing counts
exam: Which phrase means «after thinking about everything»? | Consider him a fool | Consider it done | *All things considered | Consider doing
